    {
      "name": "5. Lab 5 Grade 6 - rules caching",
      "description": "Requires cache-enabled Rules and a running application-cache Redis. Run in order, on a quiet development stack. Repeated GETs check stable data; a unique PUT followed by GET checks invalidation. The final PUT restores the captured descriptions/conditions, regenerating IDs. If interrupted, run that restore request manually. A 200 or exposed counter alone does not prove a cache hit: compare aggregated rules_cache_lookups_total{result=\"hit\"} and rules_database_loads_total across BOTH replicas in Prometheus before/after the repeat, allowing a scrape interval. Each read still makes a lightweight version query. This folder does not perform TTL/outage/concurrency tests; those are automated in the service repo.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Cache - capture current rules and warm the entry",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const rules = pm.response.json().rules;",
                  "pm.test('rules are an array', () => pm.expect(rules).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lab5_cache_original', JSON.stringify(rules));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lab5_cache_restore_payload', JSON.stringify({rules: rules.map(r => ({description:r.description, condition:r.condition}))}));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/rules",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rules"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Cache - repeat the read",
